Inside `ui/common/src`, `ui/web/src`, and `ui/mobile/src`, the category folders are
siblings, but imports between them are restricted to one direction. See
`docs/assets/ui-architecture.drawio` for the diagram.

Layers, lowest to highest:

1. `design-system` — tokens and `Option` only
2. `chassis`, `motion`
3. `hud` — shape primitives
4. `gizmos` — interactive controls, `color-box`, and `tooltip`
5. `rigs` — `popup`, `dialog`, `tabstrip`, `menu`
6. `forms`
7. `assemblies` — higher-order composites that compose gizmos/forms
   (`theme-mode-toggle`, `theme-select`)

Rules:

- A layer may import from any layer below it. A layer must never import from a
  layer above it.
- `design-system` must import nothing from the other `ui` layers. It holds tokens
  and shared primitives, not widgets.
- Use the `@package-name` alias across workspaces; use relative imports only
  within the current workspace.
- A shared component lives in `@ui/common` (API and logic); platform renderers
  live in `@ui/web` / `@ui/mobile`.
